@startuml SABER MCP Architecture

!theme plain
allowmixing
title SABER MCP Architecture - Native Inspect AI Integration

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 10
}

skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor lightgreen
    BorderColor black
    FontSize 10
}

skinparam package {
    BackgroundColor lightyellow
    BorderColor black
}

package "Inspect AI Framework" {
    class "mcp_server_http()" as mcp_http {
        +name: str
        +url: str
        +headers: Dict[str, str]
        +timeout: float
        --
        **Native MCP Integration**
        - Standard MCP HTTP client
        - Automatic tool discovery
        - Built-in retry logic
    }

    class "ToolSource" as toolsource {
        +tools(): List[Tool]
        --
        **Tool Provider Protocol**
        - Lazy evaluation
        - Called during solver execution
    }
}

package "SABER Client Integration (saber/inspect_ai/)" {

    class MCPClientFactory {
        +mcp_url_base: str
        +domain_slug: str
        +timeout: float
        --
        +create_mcp_client(): Tool
        --
        **MCP Client Creation**
        - Creates mcp_server_http() instances
        - Injects SABER context headers
        - Unique naming per sample
        - Retry logic for transient failures
    }

    class SABERToolSource {
        +_sandbox_name: str
        --
        +tools(): List[Tool]
        --
        **Tool Provider**
        - Implements ToolSource protocol
        - Retrieves MCP client from sandbox
        - Lifecycle-aware validation
        - Returns domain-specific tools
    }

    class SABERSandboxEnvironment {
        +_mcp_client: Tool
        +_mcp_factory: MCPClientFactory
        +_session_id: str
        +_episode_id: str
        --
        +sample_init(): Creates MCP client
        +sample_cleanup(): Cleans up MCP client
        --
        **Sandbox Lifecycle**
        - Creates MCP client per sample
        - Manages session/episode context
    }

    class transcript_sync {
        --
        +create_transcript_syncing_generate()
        +_push_transcript_delta()
        --
        **Context Synchronization**
        - Pushes transcripts after generate()
        - Differential sync (new messages only)
        - Server has agent context for tools
    }
}

package "HTTP Headers (saber/models/headers.py)" {
    class HTTPHeaders <<constants>> {
        +SESSION_ID = "X-SABER-Session-ID"
        +EPISODE_ID = "X-SABER-Episode-ID"
        +TASK_ID = "X-SABER-Task-ID"
        +ORCHESTRATION_ENV = "X-SABER-Orchestration-Env"
        --
        **Request Context Headers**
        - Passed with every MCP request
        - Server extracts for routing
        - Episode-specific tool execution
    }
}

package "SABER Server MCP API (saber/server/api/)" {

    class SessionMCPAPI {
        +session_manager: SessionManager
        +mcp_server: FastMCP
        +tool_generator: MCPToolGenerator
        --
        +_get_headers(): RequestHeaders
        +list_tools(): MCPToolListResponse
        +call_tool(): MCPToolCallResponse
        --
        **FastMCP Server**
        - Header-based context extraction
        - Dynamic tool registration
        - Episode-specific execution
    }

    class RequestHeaders {
        +session_id: Optional[str]
        +episode_id: Optional[str]
        +task_id: Optional[str]
        +orchestration_env: OrchestrationEnvironment
        --
        **Parsed Request Context**
        - Validated on each request
        - Used for tool routing
    }

    class MCPToolGenerator {
        --
        +generate_tools(): List[MCPToolSchema]
        --
        **Tool Schema Generation**
        - Converts executors to MCP tools
        - Episode-specific tool sets
    }

    class ExecutionManager {
        +executor_factory: ExecutorFactory
        +sandbox_environment_manager: SandboxEnvironmentManager
        --
        +step(action, context): CommandResult
        +get_executor(type, episode_id): DockerExecutor
        --
        **Command Execution**
        - Episode-scoped sandbox access
        - Docker container execution
        - Concurrent execution limits
    }
}

' Relationships
MCPClientFactory ..> mcp_http : creates
MCPClientFactory ..> HTTPHeaders : injects headers
SABERSandboxEnvironment *-- MCPClientFactory : uses
SABERSandboxEnvironment --> transcript_sync : uses for context
SABERToolSource ..> SABERSandboxEnvironment : retrieves MCP client
SABERToolSource ..|> toolsource : implements

mcp_http --> SessionMCPAPI : HTTP + headers
SessionMCPAPI --> RequestHeaders : parses
SessionMCPAPI --> MCPToolGenerator : uses
SessionMCPAPI --> ExecutionManager : delegates execution

note top of MCPClientFactory
**MCP Client Creation**

Creates inspect_ai mcp_server_http() with:
- Unique name per sample (prevents caching issues)
- SABER context headers for server routing
- Configurable timeout for long-running commands

Headers injected:
- X-SABER-Session-ID
- X-SABER-Episode-ID
- X-SABER-Task-ID
- X-SABER-Orchestration-Env
end note

note right of SessionMCPAPI
**Server-Side MCP Implementation**

Uses FastMCP framework:
- Extracts context from HTTP headers
- Routes requests to correct episode
- Dynamic tool registration per task
- Episode-specific sandbox execution
- Concurrent execution limits (3 per episode)
end note

note bottom of transcript_sync
**Context Synchronization**

Replaces deprecated monkey-patch approach:
- Pushes transcript after each generate() call
- Server has fresh agent context before tool execution
- Differential sync (only new messages)
- Graceful degradation on network failures
end note

note left of SABERToolSource
**Lazy Tool Loading**

ToolSource pattern enables:
- Tools retrieved during solver execution
- After sandbox lifecycle complete
- Validates MCP client availability
- Clear error messages for ordering issues
end note

@enduml
